    "problem": "Current global climate models have substantial uncertainties because their coarse resolution is insufficient to simulate crucial, small-scale processes like cloud convection, forcing reliance on simplified approximations that are the main source of error in climate projections.",
    "method": "The author proposes establishing international supercomputing centers to build high-resolution, kilometre-scale global climate models capable of explicitly simulating small-scale processes like cloud formation to reduce uncertainties in climate projections.",
    "task": "The task is to advocate for establishing international supercomputing centers to build high-resolution, kilometre-scale global climate models in order to substantially reduce the major uncertainties in global warming projections.",
